!x!<%#
!x!NOTE:  For HeatExchanger controls to work properly must also set the appropriate controls
!x!on Controller:OutdoorAir.  Specifically Economizer Control Type should be set to FixedDryBulb
!x!(or similar--just not NoEconomizer, even if it's a DOAS).  Economizer Maximum and Minimum Limit
!x!Dry-Bulb Temperatures are used to define when the HeatExchanger should run.
!x!Economizer Control Types for DifferentialDryBulb and DifferentialEnthalpy can also be used.
!x!
!x!UPDATE:  Default behavior for the HeatExchanger is to turn off when the Controller:OutdoorAir
!x!activates economizing.  To get the HeatExchanger to run, Economizer Lockout must be set to No.
!x!In this case, it appears that Supply Air Outlet Temperature Control frequently does not work
!x!correctly!  The HeatExchanger sometimes overheats beyond the OutdoorAirPretreat setpoint
!x!requiring extra cooling.  There is no apparent workaround.
!x!
!x!UPDATE:  An economizer control other than "NoEconomizer" on Controller:OutdoorAir is required
!x!in order to activate the economizer controls that allow heat recovery to be locked out.  When
!x!the outdoor temperature is warm enough that heat recovery would result in unnecessary cooling,
!x!it should be locked out.  Economizer Lockout must be set to "Yes" for the HeatExchanger.
!x!%>

