!x!<%#
!x!NOTE: There is a problem with the controls on HeatExchanger:AirToAir:SensibleAndLatent. The bypass controls only
!x!appear to work if an economizer is enabled AND actively operating. Otherwise the Supply Air Outlet Temperature Control
!x!is ignored, even with the proper setpoint manager.
!x!
!x!In general, this means that energy recovery WITHOUT an economizer is a bad combination. Under some conditions the
!x!energy recovery wheel will overheat the outdoor air and result in unnecessary cooling. There is no apparent
!x!workaround, although an EMS override might be possible.
!x!
!x!For DOAS--which does not normally economize--Economizer Control Type should be set to FixedDryBulb (or similar--
!x!just not NoEconomizer) in order to use energy recovery. ALSO (need to recheck): Setting the Economizer Minimum Limit
!x!to SAT - 1.0 C (roughly optimal), disables the economizer below this value and allows heat recovery to operate; above
!x!the value locks it out.
!x!%>
!x!
